  "story": {
    "logline": "A woman spends six years building a sailing boat in a garden that has no sea, and the neighbours who laughed carry it to the water.",
    "synopsis": "Maren builds a wooden boat between her shed and her back door. Nobody understands it. Seasons cross the garden — frost on the ribs, paint stripped by winter, a whole summer of sanding — and the boat slowly becomes a boat. In the bridge, eleven neighbours lift it and walk it down the lane, and every person who ever asked her what it was for is under the hull. The last chorus is the water."
  },
